F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-000388","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The lipophilicity was assessed utilizing the shake flask technique. Ir-Mito1 and Ir-Mito2 were dissolved in PBS buffer at equal concentrations of 10 μM and pre-saturated with n-octanol. An equivalent amount of n-octanol solution saturated with PBS buffer was added to each compound. The mixture was shaken in the dark for 12 h at room temperature. The two phases were separated by centrifugation, and the absorbance of the compounds in the organic and aqueous phases were measured using UV–Vis spectroscopy. The log Po/w is the logarithmic ratio of the sample concentration in the organic phase to the aqueous phase."}]}